WEBVTT

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:07.640
STUDIO RIKKA

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.060
In the future, probably Japan.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.520
Robots have long been put into practical use,

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:19.970
and practical use of androids has just begun.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.470
What does this depict?

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.810
Can't you tell? It's you!?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.940
It's...me?

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.100
Right! It's a picture of you, ----!

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.350
<i>Time of Eve</i>

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.510
<i>Dad can't come home!
19th - 21st
Lunch on Sun
</i>

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.420
Customer complaints, huh?

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:53.920
I'll let everyone know.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.050
Got it.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:00.660
Rikuo?

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:01.670
Huh?

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.780
There always so many complaints?

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:04.800
You mean father?

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:05.360
Yeah.

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.730
Seems there were tons of complaints with each new model.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:09.710
Why's that?

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.940
There were lots of unhappy customers.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.700
AI wasn't nuanced like now.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:15.850
I don't get it.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.420
Like this, look...

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.860
Sammy? A drink.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.400
Green tea after your meal?

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.400
Yeah.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.200
Understood.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:27.200
See, she gives the right response to any kind of command.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.330
The old ones couldn't do that.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.000
What kind of drink, when you wanted it...

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.000
They kept asking for clarification.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.990
People got annoyed, and the androids would crash.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.590
That's ancient history, right?

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:41.320
But he said there's been lots of odd complaints recently.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.810
Like, houseroids should be banned...

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.510
or demanding deferment of disposal fees.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.090
Oh, it was one of those.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.300
...abandoned by their owners...

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.160
<i>Please cooperate with reporting abandoned robots.</i>

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.550
Seems that AI is amazing.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:01:59.120
Never heard of it.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.180
The genius scientist one?

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:00.770
That one.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.120
There's always upgrades, so it doesn't matter when you buy one.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.280
And disposal costs are so high.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.360
Seems there's ways of getting away without paying...

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.840
But how about Sato's houseroid?

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:12.650
The cute one!

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.260
That's not my type!

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.550
Unbearable.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.140
Hey, Masaki -

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.580
<i>But I want a new one.</i>

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.260
Masaki?!

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:20.550
What?

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.320
You interested in that stuff?

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.010
<i>There won't be upgrades like that for a while.</i>

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.050
No way.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.220
Don't scare me like that!

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.700
You free today?

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.390
I'm kinda busy.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:36.510
You're always busy these days.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.880
Where do you go?

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.260
Well...how to put it...

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.970
...a lively place.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.670
It's quiet.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:46.900
Well, there aren't any customers.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:47.910
Ah...

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:48.760
Huh?

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.570
Did they leave?

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.960
This place is so odd...

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:53.240
...in so many ways.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:57.050
Um, Nagi-san, how come you work here?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.760
Just call me Nagi.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.050
'Cause I like it here.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.530
And the people who come here.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:06.610
I'm sad on days like this, when I don't get to see my favorite customers.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.760
What about us...?

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:10.670
Huh? What?

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.220
Refill...

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:16.980
Oh!

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:19.290
I'll go get the beans.

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:20.500
Wait a sec.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.450
Make yourselves at home.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.880
It sure is quiet.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:33.190
<i>House rule: No discrimination between humans and robots.</i>

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.970
It's the LUH model!

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:58.540
Huh?

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.910
A houseroid from when we started elementary school.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:02.170
They're still around...

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.320
Never seen one.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.180
They never caught on.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.030
Lots of complaints that they were hard to use.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.500
<i>House rule: No discrimination between humans and robots.</i>

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.710
It's swaying all over the place.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:31.970
<i>Eve's Doll</i>

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.560
...you have an appointment here?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.320
We're customers, you know.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.640
Customers. You understand?

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.630
I am also a customer.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:42.680
Huh?

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.160
Hey, I'm Masaki.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.420
This guy's Rikuo.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:49.580
And you?

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.080
What are you doing?!

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.770
Humans usually introduce themselves!

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.230
Introducing myself means telling you my name, correct?

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.330
This one's pretending to be a human.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.320
It's following the rules.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:03.610
That's right!

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.250
It's a picture of you, ----!

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.510
My name is ----.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.780
Why do you cover your ears?

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:17.240
My self-introduction isn't complete without my name.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:22.040
In other words, I can't show that I am human.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:25.010
My name is ----.

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:27.550
That's enough. Don't force it.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.460
Regarding what?

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:29.710
I mean your self-introduction!

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.600
Why is that? Mr. Masaki just said-

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.010
<i>Humans usually introduce themselves!</i>

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.800
That is what Mr. Masaki said.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:39.180
I'd watch what you say to this one, Masaki.

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.070
So what should we do?

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:41.890
We gotta get it to introduce itself-

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.860
We gotta hear it out!

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.440
Apologies!

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.310
Go ahead!

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.570
As I said, my name is ----.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.420
It's a...fine name.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:56.380
That is what I think.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.890
My name means a lot to me.

00:05:58.050 --> 00:05:58.890
Fine, fine.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.710
Where is the restroom?

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.170
The way it's all battered up!

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.840
Why let it fall apart like that?

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.540
Should have been set to the manufacturer for repairs.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:26.940
That talk again?!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.700
Come on, this one is too much.

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.640
Rikuo!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.250
He is a customer.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.470
You know that.

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.780
Everyone who comes here gets the same treatment.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.210
Excuse me.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.030
Welcome!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.090
Your order?

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.860
Something's the matter with it.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.310
Maybe it can't make a decision.

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.430
Probably its first time.

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:54.910
Refill!

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:59.010
I will order the same as Mr. Rikuo.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.460
OK! Two Evlends!

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.520
Coffee's OK?

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:06.990
Three coffees might be too much.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.050
No, I mean the robot.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.950
That mouth is just a speaker.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:12.470
If it tries drinking like a human...

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:13.820
Then...

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.420
Hold on!

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:18.440
The Third Law of Robotics

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:20.040
A robot cannot kill itself.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.470
It must know what'll happen if it drinks.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.070
That's right!

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.730
There's no way it'll take a drink...right?

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.310
Is there a problem?

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:37.710
The coffee!

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.140
This is bad!

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.030
What are you doing?!

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:45.290
What do you mean?

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.420
Here's your Evelend!

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.550
But why!?

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.180
So this customer can drink it, obviously.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:52.140
Don't be rude.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.740
Hey! Hold on!

00:07:58.740 --> 00:07:59.320
Turn it off!

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:00.030
I've never done it before!

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.180
Make it an order! An order will work!

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:02.190
Right!

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.800
Put down the coffee! That's an order!

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.360
Why is that?

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.310
...Why?!

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:07.650
That person just said:

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:10.250
<i>So this customer can drink it, obviously.</i>

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:11.640
<i>Don't be rude.</i>

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.590
That is what she said.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:15.560
I am a customer.

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.220
Question!

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.720
What is it?

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:20.700
...errr...

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:22.030
H-how old are you?

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:23.790
You mean my age, right?

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.030
I turn 8 this year.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:27.100
Huh?

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:27.990
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.900
Probably means it was made 8 years ago.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:37.100
You are thinking I am big for an 8-year-old human.

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:37.690
No-

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.880
No, Mr. Masaki, that was the expression on your face.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:41.830
Why all the nitpicking?!

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:44.590
Nevertheless, I am 8 years old...

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:45.820
8 years old...

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:46.960
Eigh-

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:48.960
Hey, its logic and rules are in conflict.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:49.860
It can't respond.

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:50.950
What do we do?

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.150
There are lots of different 8 year olds!

00:08:55.280 --> 00:09:00.260
Do you mean there is an 8 year old human the same size as me?

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:01.200
That's right!

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.040
That is not in my data.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.470
Please tell me the details.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:05.210
Huh?

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.290
It's...it's someone who comes here a lot!

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.520
Someone who comes here, and is 8 years old, right?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.780
Their name?

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:14.680
Her name is Chi.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.310
Though she's not actually 8 yet.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:19.960
Right! She's big...her voice, that is.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.000
I am very pleased that you believe me.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.580
And your job?!

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.970
I used to help with childcare.

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:37.270
Oh?...Childcare?

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.850
Correct. The parents and one son...

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.370
Help me out here!

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:41.780
What?

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:43.060
It's rough on my own!

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.400
I am a customer.

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:01.610
Thank you for the coffee.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:10.920
The radiator...

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.440
Why'd we even bother?

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.660
Crisis over...?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.220
Excuse me...Where is Nagi?

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:19.850
I was putting this one down for a nap,

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:22.590
and ended up falling asleep myself.

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:29.620
There's something weird sitting here!

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.690
Don't say things like that, Chie!

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:32.630
Chi, let's go home.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:33.370
I'm a cat!

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:34.370
Excuse me.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:35.540
<i>Her name is Chi-</i>

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.760
Chi, meaning the person under 8 years of age?

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:42.650
This! This is Chi!

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:45.160
What are you talking about?

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:46.310
I'm a cat!

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:47.290
She's a cat!

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:48.750
It's just something she likes to say...

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.700
She's a cat, OK!?

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.300
She says she's a cat, so she's a cat, OK?

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.030
OK!

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:52.780
I'm a cat!

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:57.000
I'll show you to the door!

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.420
Goodbye!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.340
Just now, the information was quite confusing-

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:03.330
Are you all right?!

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:05.600
Look what I found.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.170
Can I help at all?

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.200
Just leave, please.

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:11.980
How is it?

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:12.820
Can it be fixed?

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:14.810
It's already...

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.170
Thanks, Rikuo. But...

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.000
We might as well all sit down and have a nice chat.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:30.050
So you worked at their house all that time.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.540
Yes. That was where I worked.

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:37.530
I was employed to look after their son,

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:42.300
but the child has grown up, so I'm not needed.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:44.280
Did you like it there?

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:50.620
Yes. I still remember when the child gave me my name.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.460
<i>Katoran</i>

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.090
My name is very important-

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.390
And his name? What was the child's name?

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:57.910
The child...

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:00.800
was named ---.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:08.310
Their last name? Address? Contact information?

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.160
You were...

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:18.330
After all!

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.060
I am grateful to you for asking my name.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.660
<i>Everyone who comes here is treated the same.</i>

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:35.650
You are the one who invited me here, right?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:36.680
Huh?

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.950
<i>Katoran</i>

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:44.080
Please do not forget my name.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:47.540
Right! It's a picture of you, Katoran!

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.720
It's broken...?

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.490
Disposed of illegally...

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:06.100
Huh?

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:10.760
When a new robot is bought, the owner has the maker collect the old one...

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.530
But the disposal fee...

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.730
They don't want to pay, so they erase all personal information...

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:22.210
Just wanted to be remembered by someone...

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:24.290
...Its own name...

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:28.740
So it kept running from the Ethics Committee.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.080
I'm not so sure...

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:38.210
...I mean, we couldn't understand his name.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.420
That was probably erased too.

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:42.560
Such a robot thing to do.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:45.610
Lost its name ages ago but didn't even notice.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.010
...But its name was always somewhere in its heart.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:52.000
The treasured memory of receiving the name.

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.210
Heart? What's a heart, anyway?

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:54.660
Masaki!

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.350
You used to say it too, right?

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:59.140
They don't have a heart, so how can they understand music, right?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.770
...You're always wallowing like that.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.140
For god's sake!

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.640
Well it's not...normal.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.590
Right?

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:20.190
You too...?

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:44.350
<i>Ethics Committee - Vagrant robot information form</i>

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.680
The Committee's also disposing vagrant robots.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:50.000
I have nothing to do with it.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:57.830
She ignored us after all.

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:59.250
That's normal.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:02.060
Sammy's like that at home.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:04.440
Why's she only different at the cafe?

